# Responsive UI (mobile · tablet · desktop)

Design mobile-first. Every screen must work at ~360px, ~768px, and ≥1024px.

## Breakpoints (Tailwind)

| Token | Min width | Use for |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| default | 0 | phones |
| `sm:` | 640px | large phones |
| `md:` | 768px | tablets |
| `lg:` | 1024px | desktop |
| `xl:` | 1280px | wide desktop |

Prefer `md:` for tablet layout shifts and `lg:` for desktop-only chrome (sidebar).

## Layout

- Page shell: content `px-4 sm:px-6 md:px-8`, `max-w-*`; avoid fixed widths for charts
- Stack on mobile (`flex-col`); row/grid from `md:` or `lg:`
- Stats/grids: `grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3` / `xl:grid-cols-4`
- Sticky headers: keep height compact on mobile; hide secondary text until `sm:`/`md:`
- No horizontal scroll — wrap / truncate long labels

## Typography & touch

- Body readable at 14–16px; inputs ≥16px on mobile where needed
- Tap targets ≥ 44px
- Sidebar may collapse / overlay on small screens

## Motion

- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for decorative animations
